## Vendored tree-sitter Mermaid grammar

Macros bundles the C source of the **tree-sitter-mermaid** grammar
(Copyright (c) 2023 monaqa), compiled into the binary by `build.rs`. It is
licensed under the **MIT License**; the full text ships in the repository at
[`grammars/tree-sitter-mermaid/LICENSE`](grammars/tree-sitter-mermaid/LICENSE).
Unlike the other grammars (which arrive as Rust crates and are covered by
[`THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md`](THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md)), Mermaid has no crate
exposing the modern API against tree-sitter 0.26, so its source is vendored
directly. The highlight queries under `grammars/queries/` are derived from
[nvim-treesitter](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter)
(Apache-2.0).

## Rust dependencies

Macros links a large set of Rust crates — the tree-sitter grammars, the GPUI
renderer, the Steel interpreter, the Alacritty terminal core, and their
transitive dependencies. Each crate's SPDX license identifier and full license
text is reproduced in [`THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md`](THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md),
which is generated by `scripts/gen-third-party-licenses.py` (re-run it after
changing dependencies).
